{"step_index":429,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-08-20T16:25:30Z","content":"That error happened because the npm package name is **`eas-cli`** (not just `eas`). \n\nI have also pre-configured your [`app.json`](file:///C:/Users/brorm/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/snap-dialer/app.json) with an iOS bundle identifier (`com.valuteachers.snapdialer`) and created your [`eas.json`](file:///C:/Users/brorm/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/snap-dialer/eas.json) build configuration file.\n\n---\n\n### Run These Commands:\n\n#### Step 1: Log In to Expo EAS\nIn your terminal, run:\n```cmd\nnpx eas-cli login\n```\n*(If you don't have a free Expo account yet, you can sign up in 10 seconds at [expo.dev/signup](https://expo.dev/signup) or choose \"Create account\" in the prompt).*\n\n---\n\n#### Step 2: Build the iOS Standalone App\nOnce logged in, run:\n```cmd\nnpx eas-cli build --profile preview --platform ios\n```\n\n---\n\n### What Happens Next:\n1. EAS will ask: *\"Would you like to set up a project for @yourname/snap-dialer?\"* $\\rightarrow$ **Press Enter (Yes)**.\n2. It will ask to log into your Apple ID to register your test iPhone for ad-hoc internal distribution.\n3. EAS builds the iOS app in the cloud (takes ~3–5 mins) and prints a **QR code / download link** directly in your terminal.\n4. Scan the QR code with your iPhone camera to install **SnapDialer** directly onto your home screen!"}
