{"step_index":431,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-08-20T16:45:28Z","content":"**You do not need to pay Apple \\$99 to run and test this app on your iPhone.**\n\nApple restricts cloud-distributed `.ipa` files to paid accounts, but there are **two completely free, zero-cost solutions** that let you run SnapDialer on your iPhone right now:\n\n---\n\n```\n┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│                    2 100% FREE SOLUTIONS FOR YOUR IPHONE                    │\n├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│                                                                             │\n│  SOLUTION 1: Free Expo Go Cloud Relay (Most Popular & Instant)              │\n│  • Cost: $0.00 (Zero paid accounts needed).                                 │\n│  • Uses the free \"Expo Go\" app from the official iOS App Store.             │\n│  • Bypasses Apple developer fees, Microsoft Defender VPN, and firewalls.    │\n│                                                                             │\n│  SOLUTION 2: Progressive Web App (PWA) — \"Add to Home Screen\"               │\n│  • Cost: $0.00.                                                             │\n│  • Installs a real standalone app icon on your iPhone home screen.          │\n│  • Runs full-screen without Safari browser bars; triggers native SIM calls. │\n│                                                                             │\n└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n```\n\n---\n\n## Solution 1: Expo Go via Free Cloud Relay (Recommended)\n\nThis lets you test the app with full camera scanning, haptics, and native SIM dialing for **\\$0**.\n\n### Step 1: Install Expo Go on your iPhone\nDownload the free **Expo Go** app from the iOS App Store (if you haven't already).\n\n### Step 2: On your Windows PC\nIn your `snap-dialer` folder, run:\n```cmd\ncd C:\\Users\\brorm\\.gemini\\antigravity\\scratch\\snap-dialer\nnpx expo start --tunnel\n```\n*(If prompted to install `@expo/ngrok`, press **Y**).*\n\n### Step 3: Open on iPhone\n1. Open the **Camera** app or **Expo Go** on your iPhone.\n2. Scan the **QR Code** displayed in your PC terminal.\n3. **SnapDialer** opens immediately on your phone!\n\n---\n\n## Solution 2: \"Add to Home Screen\" Standalone App\n\nIf you want a permanent app icon on your iPhone home screen that opens full-screen (without Safari toolbars):\n\n1. On your PC, make sure the web preview is running:\n   ```cmd\n   npx expo start --web\n   ```\n2. Open **Safari** on your iPhone and go to your PC's IP address (e.g. `http://192.168.1.169:8081`).\n3. Tap the **Share** button (the square with an arrow pointing up at the bottom of Safari).\n4. Tap **\"Add to Home Screen\"**.\n5. A **SnapDialer** app icon will appear on your iPhone home screen. When tapped, it opens as a clean standalone app with native SIM dialing and SMS drafting!\n\n---\n\nWould you like to start **Solution 1 (Expo Go)** or **Solution 2 (Home Screen App)**?","thinking":"**Investigating Apple Error**\n\nOkay, I'm now looking into an authentication error with the Apple Developer Portal. The key issue appears to be an association problem; it seems there's no team associated with the Apple account, which is blocking progress. This is preventing further action; I need an alternative approach, as I'm not planning paid development.\n\n\n**Exploring Free Distribution Methods**\n\nI've been examining free distribution options, and I've found that I definitely do *not* need a paid Apple Developer account to test on my iPhone! I'm now investigating three completely free solutions. I am particularly interested in **Solution 1:** using Expo Go via a free cloud tunnel. It seems straightforward: just install Expo Go, run `npx expo start --tunnel`, and scan the QR code to load the app with all features active.\n\n\n"}
