{"step_index":433,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-08-20T16:47:02Z","content":"I completely understand your frustration. You want a **real app on your phone that you can take anywhere, without having your computer on, without keeping terminal windows open, and without paying Apple \\$99.**\n\nHere is the exact way to achieve a **100% standalone setup on your iPhone with zero PC connection needed**:\n\n---\n\n```\n┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│                 100% STANDALONE ON YOUR IPHONE (NO PC NEEDED)               │\n├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│                                                                             │\n│  METHOD 1: 1-Click Free Cloud Hosting (Fastest — 2 Minutes)                 │\n│  • We deploy the app to a free, private HTTPS link (e.g. Vercel/Netlify).   │\n│  • You open the link on your iPhone, tap \"Add to Home Screen\".              │\n│  • Installs as a standalone full-screen app icon on your iPhone.            │\n│  • Turns your PC OFF — runs 100% independently anywhere on cellular data.   │\n│  • Full camera scanning, local SQLite storage, and native SIM dialing/SMS.  │\n│                                                                             │\n│  METHOD 2: Free USB Sideloading (Sideloadly / AltStore)                     │\n│  • Uses Apple's free personal developer privilege (no $99 fee).             │\n│  • Plugs your iPhone into your PC once to push the compiled native app.     │\n│  • Runs standalone on your phone without the PC afterwards.                 │\n│                                                                             │\n└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n```\n\n---\n\n### Method 1: The 2-Minute Free Cloud Deploy (Recommended)\n\nThis gives you a permanent, standalone app on your iPhone that works anywhere with **zero PC dependency**:\n\n1. We export your production web build:\n   ```cmd\n   cd C:\\Users\\brorm\\.gemini\\antigravity\\scratch\\snap-dialer\n   npx expo export -p web\n   ```\n2. We deploy the resulting `dist` folder to a free hosting service (like **Vercel** or **Netlify** or **Cloudflare Pages** by running `npx vercel` or drag-and-drop).\n3. You get a private link like `https://snap-dialer-valuteachers.vercel.app`.\n4. On your iPhone:\n   - Open that link in Safari.\n   - Tap **Share (square with arrow) $\\rightarrow$ Add to Home Screen**.\n5. **You can now shut down your PC entirely.** \n   - Tap the **SnapDialer** icon on your iPhone home screen.\n   - It opens full-screen like any App Store app, accesses your camera, stores your leads locally on your device, and triggers native phone calls and texts through your carrier SIM!\n\n---\n\n### Method 2: Free USB App Push (Sideloadly)\n\nIf you want the compiled binary `.ipa` installed:\n1. We generate the native iOS build bundle locally.\n2. You plug your iPhone into your PC via USB cable.\n3. Use the free tool **Sideloadly** to sign the app with your standard free Apple ID and install it directly to your iPhone.\n4. Unplug your phone — it is now installed as a native app on your phone.\n\n---\n\nWould you like me to build and export the production package right now for **Method 1** so you can get the independent app on your iPhone in under 2 minutes?","thinking":"**Analyzing User Frustration**\n\nI'm trying to dissect the user's frustration regarding the app testing setup. They're clearly unhappy with the current PC link and desperately want to test the full app on their personal phone. My focus is now on understanding the core reason for this desire and pinpointing the specific limitations of the current method that are causing this dissatisfaction.\n\n\n**Exploring Standalone Solutions**\n\nI've been exploring ways to achieve a truly independent iPhone app, focusing on avoiding the \\$99/year Apple Developer fee. The goal is a completely computer-free setup. I'm currently assessing the feasibility of a 1-Click Free Cloud Web Deploy PWA using platforms like Vercel, Netlify, or Cloudflare Pages. This approach seems promising, enabling a standalone app experience via \"Add to Home Screen\" functionality, and all for free.\n\n\n"}
