o surge or no?\n\n# Previous Session Summary:\nNo, changes made locally on your PC **will not automatically update the live Surge site until you re-export and re-publish**. \n\nWhenever we make changes or add features, it only takes a **single 10-second command** to update your live app:\n\n```cmd\nnpm run deploy\n```\n*(Or manually: `npx expo export -p web` followed by `npx surge ./dist valuteachers-dialer.surge.sh`).*\n\nOnce published, you simply open the app on your iPhone or pull-to-refresh, and it instantly loads the newest version!\n\n---\n\n# Continuation Summary\n\n## 1. Outstanding User Requests\n- **Deploy Automation Script:**\n  - *User Directive:* `\"going forward, as we make changes, will they automatically be published to surge or no?\"`\n  - *Status:* **IMPLEMENTATION** (Explain deployment lifecycle and add a 1-step `npm run deploy` script in `package.json`).\n- **Live User Beta Testing Feedback:**\n  - *User Directive:* `\"that worked...i'm able to do some testing now.\"`\n  - *Status:* **AWAITING USER FEEDBACK** (Awaiting real-world feedback from the user's test dialing and scanning session on their iPhone).\n\n---\n\n## 2. User Knowledge\n- **Domain & Goals:**\n  - Target company: **ValuTeachers** working with Florida educators on the **Florida Retirement System (FRS)** and **403(b)/457(b)** retirement plans.\n  - Primary call objective: **To schedule a full 45-minute planning period sit-down** (preferably in their classroom during their scheduled planning window).\n  - Quote on Meeting Duration: `\"much better, but our meetings generally run the entire 45min planning session. i do like the tone and format of the message in this latest example\"`\n  - Quote on Cost & Independence: `\"I will not be paying to develop apps for my own use. I'll need another solution\"`, `\"this stinks! I want to test the full app running on my personal phone...i do not want this pc link setup\"`.\n  - Deployment Choice: User chose Surge static publishing to run SnapDialer as an independent standalone PWA on iPhone.\n  - Live Surge Domain: Published and active on Surge (e.g., `valuteachers-dialer.surge.sh`).\n\n---\n\n## 3. Work Accomplished\n1. **Document Ingestion & On-Device Downsampling Pipeline:**\n   - Built `DocumentScannerService.ts`: Uses native iOS VisionKit / Android ML Kit in native dev builds with interactive fallback (`allowsEditing: true`).\n   - Slashes raw 48MP photos (8MB–12MB) to 1600px width at 0.75 JPEG compression (<250KB) on-device before API encoding.\n2. **1-Tap \"View Original Report Card (Proof of Request)\" Modal:**\n   - Permanent storage of scanned document photos in device sandbox; SQLite stores `source_image_uri`.\n   - 1-tap modal in `DialerHudScreen.tsx` and `LeadDetailScreen.tsx` for real-time handwriting double-checking and express consent verification.\n3. **Gemini 2.5 Flash AI Persuasive SMS Engine:**\n   - Built `AiSmsService.ts`: Context-aware copywriting synthesized from educator profile, checked report card needs, requested availability, and full history of past call logs and notes.\n   - Tailored specifically to schedule **on-campus 45-minute planning period sit-downs**.\n   - 100% editable preview modal with 1-tap focus presets (*Meeting Slot*, *5% Bonus & DROP*, *Planning Period*).\n4. **Standalone iPhone Home Screen Deployment:**\n   - Generated production `dist` web bundle with standalone PWA meta tags (`apple-mobile-web-app-capable`, `manifest.json`).\n   - Successfully deployed via Surge; live and independently running on user's personal iPhone.\n\n---\n\n## 4. Model Knowledge\n- **PWA on iOS:**\n  - Safari \"Add to Home Screen\" opens full-screen without URL bars when `apple-mobile-web-app-capable` is set to `yes`.\n  - Native telephone (`tel:`) and SMS (`sms:`) URL schemes trigger the native iOS Phone and Messages apps directly from the PWA.\n- **Surge Re-Deployment Workflow:**\n  - To push updates: `npx expo export -p web` $\\rightarrow$ `npx surge ./dist <domain>`.\n\n---\n\n## 5. Files and Code\n\n### Edited Files\n- `src/services/aiSmsService.ts`: AI copywriting engine synthesized from lead history and report card notes, calibrated for 45-minute planning session sit-downs.\n- `src/services/documentScannerService.ts`: Native document scanner wrapper and universal <250KB image downsampler.\n- `src/services/visionService.ts`: Integrated `DocumentScannerService` for on-device downsampling before Gemini API transmission.\n- `src/types/index.ts`: Added `source_image_uri` to `Lead` and `ExtractedLeadItem`.\n- `src/db/database.ts`: Added `source_image_uri` column to `leads` table and updated pre-seeded SMS templates with planning period sit-down phrasing.\n- `src/db/leadsRepository.ts`: Hydration and persistence of `source_image_uri`.\n- `src/screens/DialerHudScreen.tsx`: Added Proof of Contact image viewer modal and Gemini AI SMS drafting with editable modal.\n- `src/screens/LeadDetailScreen.tsx`: Added Proof of Contact image viewer and AI SMS drafting.\n- `src/screens/ScanSheetScreen.tsx`: Integrated `DocumentScannerService` and verification inputs for ValuTeachers fields.\n- `dist/index.html` & `dist/manifest.json`: Added iOS standalone PWA tags and manifest.\n- `app.json` & `eas.json`: Added iOS bundle identifier and EAS configuration.\n\n---\n\n## 6. Current Work and Next Steps\n1. Add a `\"deploy\": \"expo export -p web && surge ./dist valuteachers-dialer.surge.sh\"` convenience script to `package.json`.\n2. Await the user's live testing feedback from their iPhone beta test and implement any requested UI/UX or workflow tweaks.\n\nYou have the 4 following artifacts written to the artifacts directory:\n\n[ARTIFACT: media_1787239731075]\nPath: file:///C:/Users/brorm/.gemini/antigravity/brain/9c9b5ef4-82a1-483f-9e9e-cb421c9396b3/.user_uploaded/media_1787239731075.jpg\nLast Edited: 2026-08-20T15:30:15Z\n\n[ARTIFACT: media_1787239731084]\nPath: file:///C:/Users/brorm/.gemini/antigravity/brain/9c9b5ef4-82a1-483f-9e9e-cb421c9396b3/.user_uploaded/